---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import Demo from '../../components/Demo.astro'
import CollapseBasic from '../../demos/collapse-basic.vue'
import MagneticBasic from '../../demos/magnetic-basic.vue'
import PhotoPileBasic from '../../demos/photo-pile-basic.vue'
import RevealBasic from '../../demos/reveal-basic.vue'
import ScribbleHighlightBasic from '../../demos/scribble-highlight-basic.vue'
import StickerBurstBasic from '../../demos/sticker-burst-basic.vue'
import TextBloomBasic from '../../demos/text-bloom-basic.vue'
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'installation', text: 'Installation' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'reveal', text: 'Reveal' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'collapse', text: 'Collapse' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'text-bloom', text: 'TextBloom' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'magnetic', text: 'Magnetic' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'photo-pile', text: 'PhotoPile' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'scribble-highlight', text: 'ScribbleHighlight' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'sticker-burst', text: 'StickerBurst' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'support', text: 'Support and rendering' },
]
const stylesImport = "import '@kida-ui/styles/kida.css'"
---

<DocsLayout title="Vue (experimental)" description="All seven Kida animations for Vue 3.5, using the shared motion and styles." currentPath="/docs/vue" headings={headings}>
  <p>Vue support includes Reveal, Collapse, TextBloom, Magnetic, PhotoPile, ScribbleHighlight, and StickerBurst.</p>
  <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
  <p>The Vue package covers seven shared components. <a href="/docs/dual-wave">DualWave</a> currently supports React only. npm publication is pending; after release, install the adapter and shared styles:</p>
  <CodeBlock code="pnpm add @kida-ui/vue @kida-ui/styles" lang="bash" />
  <p>Import the styles once in your application entry:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={stylesImport} lang="ts" />
  <p>Vue 3.5 or later in the Vue 3 series is required. The existing shadcn registry installs React components; Vue copied-source installation is not yet available.</p>
  <h2 id="reveal">Reveal</h2>
  <Demo name="reveal-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue Reveal">
    <RevealBasic client:visible={{ rootMargin: '200px' }} />
  </Demo>
  <p>Use the default slot for content and native <code>class</code>, <code>style</code>, attributes, and events on the root. Motion options and defaults match <a href="/docs/reveal">Reveal's API</a>. Bind Boolean options explicitly, such as <code>:once="false"</code>. The <code>as</code> prop accepts an HTML tag name.</p>
  <h2 id="collapse">Collapse</h2>
  <Demo name="collapse-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue Collapse">
    <CollapseBasic client:visible />
  </Demo>
  <p>Control visibility with <code>:open</code> and listen to <code>@exit-complete</code>. The event fires after the exit completes and presence removes the panel. Use the default slot for content. The CSS custom properties match <a href="/docs/collapse">Collapse's API</a>.</p>
  <p>Place visual padding and borders on the inner content so the collapsing root can shrink to zero.</p>
  <h2 id="text-bloom">TextBloom</h2>
  <Demo name="text-bloom-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue TextBloom">
    <TextBloomBasic client:visible={{ rootMargin: '200px' }} />
  </Demo>
  <p>Pass plain text with the required <code>text</code> prop instead of a slot. Use <code>by="word"</code> or <code>by="character"</code> and <code>voice="gentle"</code> or <code>voice="pop"</code>. Character mode splits Unicode code points, not grapheme clusters. Changing text, segmentation, or motion options cancels the previous pass and animates the new text. Change the component's <code>key</code> to replay unchanged text.</p>
  <p>The HTML <code>as</code> prop and remaining motion options match <a href="/docs/text-bloom">TextBloom's API</a>. The rendered text appears once in authored order, preserving whitespace, selection, and screen-reader access.</p>
  <h2 id="magnetic">Magnetic</h2>
  <Demo name="magnetic-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue Magnetic">
    <MagneticBasic client:visible />
  </Demo>
  <p>Put your native button or link in the default slot. <code>strength</code> and <code>maxDistance</code> match <a href="/docs/magnetic">Magnetic's API</a>; <code>targetClass</code> (or <code>target-class</code> in templates) styles the moving inner span. Root classes and attributes apply to the stationary wrapper. Keyboard activation and child events remain native; touch movement does not pull the target.</p>
  <h2 id="photo-pile">PhotoPile</h2>
  <Demo name="photo-pile-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue PhotoPile">
    <PhotoPileBasic client:visible />
  </Demo>
  <p>Bind a <code>photos</code> array with unique stable <code>id</code>, <code>src</code>, and <code>alt</code> fields. Each photo accepts optional <code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, <code>rotation</code>, and native Vue image attributes in <code>imageProps</code>. The demo's images are served from <code>/demo</code>; use your own image URLs in an application.</p>
  <p><code>spread</code>, <code>dragScale</code>, and <code>tilt</code> match <a href="/docs/photo-pile">PhotoPile's API</a>. Use <code>aria-label</code> to name the group. Focus raises a photo to the front. Reordering or replacing photos cancels an active gesture and binds the new collection. Classes, alt text, and layout offsets update without resetting the current layer. Keep padding and borders on the inner photo cards.</p>
  <h2 id="scribble-highlight">ScribbleHighlight</h2>
  <Demo name="scribble-highlight-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue ScribbleHighlight">
    <ScribbleHighlightBasic client:visible />
  </Demo>
  <p>Wrap readable content in the default slot. <code>variant="underline"</code> or <code>variant="circle"</code>, <code>once</code>, and <code>amount</code> match <a href="/docs/scribble-highlight">ScribbleHighlight's API</a>. The decorative SVG is hidden from assistive technology.</p>
  <h2 id="sticker-burst">StickerBurst</h2>
  <Demo name="sticker-burst-basic" framework="vue" title="Vue StickerBurst">
    <StickerBurstBasic client:visible />
  </Demo>
  <p>Place a native button or link in the default slot. Clicks, including keyboard-generated clicks, replay the decorative burst while preserving authored handlers. <code>stickers</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>distance</code>, and <code>seed</code> match <a href="/docs/sticker-burst">StickerBurst's API</a>. Layouts are deterministic, empty sticker arrays use the default symbols, and the decorative layer is hidden from screen readers.</p>
  <h2 id="support">Support and rendering</h2>
  <p>All seven components render deterministic server HTML and hydrate on the client. Under reduced motion, Reveal and TextBloom remain visible before hydration, Collapse exits immediately, and decorative and pointer effects settle without animated movement. PhotoPile remains focusable and interactive.</p>
  <p>Vue component refs expose an <code>element</code> property containing the DOM root. For Collapse it becomes <code>null</code> after an exit. Changing motion options replaces Reveal's controller; changes to slot content or an equivalent easing tuple preserve its current animation.</p>
  <p>The milestone is experimental. Chromium browser behavior, Node SSR, hydration, mobile and desktop layout, accessibility rules, and packed-package consumption are checked. Manual screen-reader and touch checks and a wider browser matrix remain release work.</p>
</DocsLayout>
